IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa17-helpers`

-- coa17-part21a-ch2a-id.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 21A, Chapter 2A -- Identity verification obligations
-- for persons with significant control (ss 790LM to 790LT; lines 10565-10680 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law,
-- objectively. SOURCE, TARGET and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER are as in coa17-part21-ch1.l4 (JUST TRUE: the text says yes; JUST
-- FALSE: the text says no in its own words; NOTHING: the text does not decide; a caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE).
--
-- THE GATE. `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` (MAYBE BOOLEAN) as in the other Chapter 2 and 2A modules (fork F4).
-- SEAMS (PLAN.md section 4). `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified` (coa24, MAYBE BOOLEAN) and `s 1121 the officer is
-- in default` (coa24). Sections 12A and 12B (coa1) and 790LG (this part) are facts here.
-- DATES the Act does not give are INPUTS: "the appointed day" (appointed by regulations), and the days on which sections 12B(2)
-- and (3) and 790LB(1) and (2) came fully into force.
-- TEXT TRAPS, encoded as written and listed in NOTES.md ("What the text turns out to say"): s 790LM(1) Case 2(a) says the
-- registrar "is notified under section 790LF that a person has become a registrable person" (790LF is the notice of
-- ceasing; the notice of becoming is 790LA); s 790LR(3)(a)(iii) says "the direction 790LO" with no "under section".
-- NOT ENCODED HERE: nothing is machinery; s 790LN and s 790LP are transitional but a person can be bound by them, so they are encoded.

-- FORKS in this module (NOTES.md, "Fork register (coa17)", gives each reading and the text that licenses it; the
-- coverage table points each row at its fork): F1 at s 790LM(2), s 790LN(3), s 790LO(2), s 790LP(3); F5 at s
-- 790LM(4), s 790LO(4), s 790LS(2), s 790LS(3); F6 at s 790LM(5), s 790LO(5); F8 at s 790LM(1), s 790LO(1); F11 at s
-- 790LT(1); F14 at s 790LM(1) Case 2(a), s 790LR(3)(a)(iii); F15 at s 790LQ(2)(b), s 790LR(3)(b).

§ `Part 21A Chapter 2A: Identity verification obligations for persons with significant control`

§§ `Initial identity verification: registrable persons (ss 790LM and 790LN)`

-- src:10568 | Case 1 is where—
-- src:10569 | (a) a company is incorporated in pursuance of an application for registration containing a statement under section 12A(1)(a) naming a person as someone who will, on the company’s incorporation, become a registrable person (“the registrable person”),
-- src:10570 | (b) the application does not include a statement under section 12B(2) in respect of the registrable person or it appears to the registrar that the statement is false, and
-- src:10571 | (c) the company has not given a notice under section 790LG(1) in respect of the person.
@ref s 790LM(1) Case 1 (src:10568-10571)
GIVEN `the company was incorporated in pursuance of an application for registration containing a statement under section 12A(1)(a) naming the person as someone who will, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application does not include a statement under section 12B(2) in respect of the registrable person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the registrar that the statement under section 12B(2) is false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has not given a notice under section 790LG(1) in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LM(1) Case 1 applies` MEANS
    IF    `the company was incorporated in pursuance of an application for registration containing a statement under section 12A(1)(a) naming the person as someone who will, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable person`
       AND (`the application does not include a statement under section 12B(2) in respect of the registrable person` OR `it appears to the registrar that the statement under section 12B(2) is false`)
       AND `the company has not given a notice under section 790LG(1) in respect of the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Case 1 is where— (a) ..., (b) ... and (c) ..." (the where condition fails)

-- src:10572 | Case 2 is where—
-- src:10573 | (a) the registrar is notified under section 790LF that a person has become a registrable person in relation to a company (“the registrable person”), and
-- src:10574 | (b) the notice does not include a statement under section 790LB(1) or it appears to the registrar that the statement is false.
@ref s 790LM(1) Case 2 (src:10572-10574)
GIVEN `the registrar is notified under section 790LF that a person has become a registrable person in relation to a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice does not include a statement under section 790LB(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the registrar that the statement under section 790LB(1) is false` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LM(1) Case 2 applies` MEANS
    IF    `the registrar is notified under section 790LF that a person has become a registrable person in relation to a company`
       AND (`the notice does not include a statement under section 790LB(1)` OR `it appears to the registrar that the statement under section 790LB(1) is false`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Case 2 is where— (a) ... and (b) ..." (the where condition fails; the text says 790LF where the notice of becoming is 790LA: encoded as written)

-- src:10575 | (2) The registrar must direct the registrable person to deliver to the registrar, within the period of 14 days beginning with the date of the direction, a statement confirming that the person’s identity is verified (see section 1110A).
@ref s 790LM(2) The registrar must direct the registrable person to deliver a statement confirming that the person's identity is verified (src:10575)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 790LM(1) for Case 1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 790LM(1) for Case 2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LM(2) the registrar must direct the registrable person to deliver a statement confirming that the person's identity is verified` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF `the person is a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “registrable person” does not include a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)." (subsection (6))
         ELSE `s 790C(7) either answer holds` `the answer under section 790LM(1) for Case 1` `the answer under section 790LM(1) for Case 2`) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies in the following cases." (neither case: fork F8)

@ref s 790LM(2) within the period of 14 days beginning with the date of the direction (src:10575)
GIVEN `the date of the direction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790LM(2) the last day for the registrable person to deliver the statement` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` `the date of the direction`

@ref s 790LM(2) the registrable person delivered the statement within the period (src:10575)
GIVEN `the date of the direction` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the registrable person delivered the statement` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LM(2) the registrable person delivered the statement in time` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` (`s 790LM(2) the last day for the registrable person to deliver the statement` `the date of the direction`) `the day on which the registrable person delivered the statement` `the day on which the question is asked` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the period of 14 days beginning with the date of the direction"

-- src:10576 | (3) The registrar may by further direction extend that period by up to 14 days at a time.
@ref s 790LM(3) The registrar may by further direction extend that period by up to 14 days at a time (src:10576)
GIVEN `the last day of the period before the extension` IS A DATE
      `the number of days by which the further direction extends the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 790LM(3) the last day of the period as extended by the further direction` MEANS
    IF `the number of days by which the further direction extends the period` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the number of days by which the further direction extends the period` AT MOST 14
    THEN JUST (`the last day of the period before the extension` PLUS `the number of days by which the further direction extends the period`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by up to 14 days at a time"

-- src:10577 | (4) A direction under this section must be in writing.
@ref s 790LM(4) A direction under this section must be in writing (src:10577)
GIVEN `the direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LM(4) the direction meets the requirement as to form` MEANS
    IF `the direction is in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A direction under this section must be in writing." (a bare must not done: fork F5)

-- src:10578 | (5) A direction given to a person under this section lapses if notice is later given under section 790LG(1) in respect of that person.
@ref s 790LM(5) A direction lapses if notice is later given under section 790LG(1) (src:10578)
GIVEN `notice is later given under section 790LG(1) in respect of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LM(5) the direction lapses` MEANS
    IF `notice is later given under section 790LG(1) in respect of that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A direction given to a person under this section lapses if notice is later given under section 790LG(1) in respect of that person." (the if fails: fork F6)

-- src:10581 | (1) A person must deliver to the registrar the statement required by this section if the person—
-- src:10582 | (a) is a registrable person in relation to a company at any time during the appointed day, and
-- src:10583 | (b) either—
-- src:10584 | (i) became a registrable person on the incorporation of the company in pursuance of an application for registration delivered before section 12B(2) came fully into force, or
-- src:10585 | (ii) became a registrable person, otherwise than on the incorporation of the company, before the day on which section 790LB(1) came fully into force.
@ref s 790LN(1) A person must deliver to the registrar the statement required by this section if the person (src:10581-10585)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a registrable person in relation to a company at any time during the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person became a registrable person on the incorporation of the company in pursuance of an application for registration delivered before section 12B(2) came fully into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person became a registrable person, otherwise than on the incorporation of the company, before the day on which section 790LB(1) came fully into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LN(1) the person must deliver to the registrar the statement required by this section` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF `the person is a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registrable person” does not include a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)." (subsection (5))
         ELSE IF    `the person is a registrable person in relation to a company at any time during the appointed day`
                AND (   `the person became a registrable person on the incorporation of the company in pursuance of an application for registration delivered before section 12B(2) came fully into force`
                     OR `the person became a registrable person, otherwise than on the incorporation of the company, before the day on which section 790LB(1) came fully into force`)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person must deliver to the registrar the statement required by this section if the person— (a) ... and (b) ..." (the if fails)

-- src:10586 | (2) The statement required by this section is a statement confirming that person’s identity is verified (see section 1110A).
@ref s 790LN(2) The statement required by this section is a statement confirming that person's identity is verified (src:10586)
GIVEN `the statement confirms that the person's identity is verified (see section 1110A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LN(2) the statement is the statement required by this section` MEANS
    IF `the statement confirms that the person's identity is verified (see section 1110A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement required by this section is a statement confirming that person’s identity is verified"

-- src:10587 | (3) A statement required by this section must be delivered within the period of 14 days beginning with the appointed day.
@ref s 790LN(3) within the period of 14 days beginning with the appointed day (src:10587)
GIVEN `the appointed day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790LN(3) the last day for the person to deliver the statement` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` `the appointed day`

@ref s 790LN(3) the person delivered the statement within the period (src:10587)
GIVEN `the appointed day` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person delivered the statement` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LN(3) the person delivered the statement in time` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` (`s 790LN(3) the last day for the person to deliver the statement` `the appointed day`) `the day on which the person delivered the statement` `the day on which the question is asked` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be delivered within the period of 14 days beginning with the appointed day"

-- src:10588 | (4) But the registrar may by direction in writing extend that period by up to 14 days at a time.
@ref s 790LN(4) But the registrar may by direction in writing extend that period by up to 14 days at a time (src:10588)
GIVEN `the last day of the period before the extension` IS A DATE
      `the number of days by which the direction extends the period` IS A NUMBER
      `the direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 790LN(4) the last day of the period as extended by the direction` MEANS
    IF `the direction is in writing` AND `the number of days by which the direction extends the period` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the number of days by which the direction extends the period` AT MOST 14
    THEN JUST (`the last day of the period before the extension` PLUS `the number of days by which the direction extends the period`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by direction in writing extend that period by up to 14 days at a time"

-- src:10589 | (5) In this section—
-- src:10590 | “the appointed day” means such day as the Secretary of State may by regulations appoint for the purposes of this section;
-- src:10591 | “registrable person” does not include a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d).
@ref s 790LN(5) "the appointed day" means such day as the Secretary of State may by regulations appoint (src:10589-10591)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day the Secretary of State appointed by regulations for the purposes of this section` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LN(5) the day is the appointed day` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` EQUALS `the day the Secretary of State appointed by regulations for the purposes of this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the appointed day” means such day as the Secretary of State may by regulations appoint for the purposes of this section"

-- src:10592 | (6) The appointed day must not be before sections 12B(2) and 790LB(1) have been brought fully into force.
@ref s 790LN(6) The appointed day must not be before sections 12B(2) and 790LB(1) have been brought fully into force (src:10592)
GIVEN `the appointed day` IS A DATE
      `the day on which sections 12B(2) and 790LB(1) had both been brought fully into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LN(6) the appointed day is not before sections 12B(2) and 790LB(1) have been brought fully into force` MEANS
    IF `the appointed day` AT LEAST `the day on which sections 12B(2) and 790LB(1) had both been brought fully into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The appointed day must not be before sections 12B(2) and 790LB(1) have been brought fully into force."

§§ `Initial identity verification: registrable relevant legal entities (ss 790LO and 790LP)`

-- src:10595 | Case 1 is where—
-- src:10596 | (a) a company is incorporated in pursuance of an application for registration containing a statement under section 12A(1)(a) naming a person as a person who will, on the company’s incorporation become a registrable relevant legal entity (“the entity”),
-- src:10597 | (b) the application does not include a statement under section 12B(3) in respect of the entity, or is not accompanied by a statement under section 12B(4) by the person whose name is specified in the statement under section 12B(3), or it appears to the registrar that either statement is false, and
-- src:10598 | (c) the company has not given a notice under section 790LG(1) in respect of the entity.
@ref s 790LO(1) Case 1 (src:10595-10598)
GIVEN `the company was incorporated in pursuance of an application for registration containing a statement under section 12A(1)(a) naming a person as a person who will, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application does not include a statement under section 12B(3) in respect of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is not accompanied by a statement under section 12B(4) by the person whose name is specified in the statement under section 12B(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the registrar that either statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has not given a notice under section 790LG(1) in respect of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LO(1) Case 1 applies` MEANS
    IF    `the company was incorporated in pursuance of an application for registration containing a statement under section 12A(1)(a) naming a person as a person who will, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable relevant legal entity`
       AND (   `the application does not include a statement under section 12B(3) in respect of the entity`
            OR `the application is not accompanied by a statement under section 12B(4) by the person whose name is specified in the statement under section 12B(3)`
            OR `it appears to the registrar that either statement is false`)
       AND `the company has not given a notice under section 790LG(1) in respect of the entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Case 1 is where— (a) ..., (b) ... and (c) ..." (the where condition fails)

-- src:10599 | Case 2 is where—
-- src:10600 | (a) the registrar is notified under section 790LA that a person has become a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company (“the entity”), and
-- src:10601 | (b) the notice does not include a statement under section 790LB(2), or it is not accompanied by a statement under section 790LB(3), or it appears to the registrar that either statement is false.
@ref s 790LO(1) Case 2 (src:10599-10601)
GIVEN `the registrar is notified under section 790LA that a person has become a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice does not include a statement under section 790LB(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is not accompanied by a statement under section 790LB(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the registrar that either statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LO(1) Case 2 applies` MEANS
    IF    `the registrar is notified under section 790LA that a person has become a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company`
       AND (   `the notice does not include a statement under section 790LB(2)`
            OR `the notice is not accompanied by a statement under section 790LB(3)`
            OR `it appears to the registrar that either statement is false`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Case 2 is where— (a) ... and (b) ..." (the where condition fails)

-- src:10602 | (2) The registrar must direct the entity to deliver to the registrar, within the period of 28 days beginning with the date of the direction—
