-- src:10610 | (6) In subsection (2) “relevant officer”—
-- src:10611 | (a) in relation to a company, means a director;
-- src:10612 | (b) in relation to a legal entity the affairs of which are managed by its members, means one of those members;
-- src:10613 | (c) in relation to any other legal entity, means an officer of the entity whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company.
@ref s 790LO(6) "relevant officer" (src:10610-10613)
DECLARE `s 790LO(6) kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `s 790LO(6)(a) a company`
    `s 790LO(6)(b) a legal entity the affairs of which are managed by its members`
    `s 790LO(6)(c) any other legal entity`

GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `s 790LO(6) kind of body`
      `the individual is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is one of the members who manage the legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is an officer of the entity whose functions correspond to those of a director of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LO(6) the individual is a relevant officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of body`
    WHEN `s 790LO(6)(a) a company` THEN
        IF `the individual is a director of the company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant officer”— (a) in relation to a company, means a director"
    WHEN `s 790LO(6)(b) a legal entity the affairs of which are managed by its members` THEN
        IF `the individual is one of the members who manage the legal entity`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in relation to a legal entity the affairs of which are managed by its members, means one of those members"
    WHEN `s 790LO(6)(c) any other legal entity` THEN
        IF `the individual is an officer of the entity whose functions correspond to those of a director of a company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) in relation to any other legal entity, means an officer of the entity whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company"

-- src:10615 | (1) A person must deliver to the registrar the statements required by this section if the person—
-- src:10616 | (a) is a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company at any time during the appointed day, and
-- src:10617 | (b) either—
-- src:10618 | (i) became a registrable relevant legal entity on the incorporation of the company in pursuance of an application for registration delivered before section 12B(3) and (4) came fully into force, or
-- src:10619 | (ii) became a registrable relevant legal entity, otherwise than on the incorporation of the company, before section 790LB(2) and (3) came fully into force.
@ref s 790LP(1) A person must deliver to the registrar the statements required by this section if the person (src:10615-10619)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company at any time during the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person became a registrable relevant legal entity on the incorporation of the company in pursuance of an application for registration delivered before section 12B(3) and (4) came fully into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person became a registrable relevant legal entity, otherwise than on the incorporation of the company, before section 790LB(2) and (3) came fully into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LP(1) the person must deliver to the registrar the statements required by this section` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF    `the person is a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company at any time during the appointed day`
           AND (   `the person became a registrable relevant legal entity on the incorporation of the company in pursuance of an application for registration delivered before section 12B(3) and (4) came fully into force`
                OR `the person became a registrable relevant legal entity, otherwise than on the incorporation of the company, before section 790LB(2) and (3) came fully into force`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person must deliver to the registrar the statements required by this section if the person— (a) ... and (b) ..." (the if fails)

-- src:10620 | (2) The statements are—
-- src:10621 | (a) a statement by the entity that—
-- src:10622 | (i) specifies the name of one of its relevant officers who is an individual and whose identity is verified, and
-- src:10623 | (ii) confirms that the individual’s identity is verified, and
-- src:10624 | (b) a statement by the individual confirming that the individual is a relevant officer of the entity.
@ref s 790LP(2) The statements are (src:10620-10624)
GIVEN `the statement by the entity specifies the name of one of its relevant officers who is an individual and whose identity is verified, and confirms that the individual's identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement by the individual confirms that the individual is a relevant officer of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LP(2) the statements delivered are the statements required by this section` MEANS
    IF    `the statement by the entity specifies the name of one of its relevant officers who is an individual and whose identity is verified, and confirms that the individual's identity is verified`
       AND `the statement by the individual confirms that the individual is a relevant officer of the entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statements are— (a) a statement by the entity that— ... and (b) a statement by the individual confirming that the individual is a relevant officer of the entity"

-- src:10625 | (3) The statements required by this section must be delivered within the period of 28 days beginning with the appointed day.
@ref s 790LP(3) within the period of 28 days beginning with the appointed day (src:10625)
GIVEN `the appointed day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790LP(3) the last day for the entity to deliver the statements` MEANS
    `s 790LO(2) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the day` `the appointed day`

@ref s 790LP(3) the entity delivered the statements within the period (src:10625)
GIVEN `the appointed day` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the entity delivered the statements` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LP(3) the entity delivered the statements in time` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` (`s 790LP(3) the last day for the entity to deliver the statements` `the appointed day`) `the day on which the entity delivered the statements` `the day on which the question is asked` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be delivered within the period of 28 days beginning with the appointed day"

-- src:10626 | (4) But the registrar may by direction in writing extend that period by up to 28 days at a time.
@ref s 790LP(4) But the registrar may by direction in writing extend that period by up to 28 days at a time (src:10626)
GIVEN `the last day of the period before the extension` IS A DATE
      `the number of days by which the direction extends the period` IS A NUMBER
      `the direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 790LP(4) the last day of the period as extended by the direction` MEANS
    IF `the direction is in writing` AND `the number of days by which the direction extends the period` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the number of days by which the direction extends the period` AT MOST 28
    THEN JUST (`the last day of the period before the extension` PLUS `the number of days by which the direction extends the period`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by direction in writing extend that period by up to 28 days at a time"

-- src:10627 | (5) In this section—
-- src:10628 | “the appointed day” means such day as the Secretary of State may by regulations appoint for the purposes of this section;
-- src:10629 | “relevant officer” has the meaning given by section 790LO(6).
@ref s 790LP(5) "the appointed day" and "relevant officer" (src:10627-10629)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day the Secretary of State appointed by regulations for the purposes of this section` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LP(5) the day is the appointed day` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` EQUALS `the day the Secretary of State appointed by regulations for the purposes of this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the appointed day” means such day as the Secretary of State may by regulations appoint for the purposes of this section"

@ref s 790LP(5) "relevant officer" has the meaning given by section 790LO(6) (src:10629)
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `s 790LO(6) kind of body`
      `the individual is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is one of the members who manage the legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is an officer of the entity whose functions correspond to those of a director of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LP(5) the individual is a relevant officer` MEANS
    `s 790LO(6) the individual is a relevant officer` `the kind of body` `the individual is a director of the company` `the individual is one of the members who manage the legal entity` `the individual is an officer of the entity whose functions correspond to those of a director of a company`

-- src:10630 | (6) The appointed day must not be before sections 12B(3) and (4) and 790LB(2) and (3) have been brought fully into force.
@ref s 790LP(6) The appointed day must not be before sections 12B(3) and (4) and 790LB(2) and (3) have been brought fully into force (src:10630)
GIVEN `the appointed day` IS A DATE
      `the day on which sections 12B(3) and (4) and 790LB(2) and (3) had all been brought fully into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LP(6) the appointed day is not before sections 12B(3) and (4) and 790LB(2) and (3) have been brought fully into force` MEANS
    IF `the appointed day` AT LEAST `the day on which sections 12B(3) and (4) and 790LB(2) and (3) had all been brought fully into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The appointed day must not be before sections 12B(3) and (4) and 790LB(2) and (3) have been brought fully into force."

§§ `Duties to maintain verified identity status (ss 790LQ to 790LS)`

-- src:10633 | (2) In this section “the relevant period” means the period—
-- src:10634 | (a) beginning with—
-- src:10635 | (i) the incorporation of the company, in a case where the person became a registrable person on its incorporation and the application for registration of the company included a statement under section 12B(2) in respect of the person,
-- src:10636 | (ii) the delivery to the registrar of a statement in respect of the person under section 790LB(1), in a case where the person became a registrable person after the incorporation of the company and such a statement was delivered to the registrar,
-- src:10637 | (iii) the expiry of the period for complying with the direction under section 790LM, in a case where a direction under that section is given to the person, and
-- src:10638 | (iv) the expiry of the period for complying with section 790LN, in a case where that section applies to the person, and
-- src:10639 | (b) ending on the giving of a notice to the registrar under section 790LF that the person has ceased to be a registrable person in relation to the company.
@ref s 790LQ(2) "the relevant period" (src:10633-10639)
DECLARE `s 790LQ(2)(a) the event with which the relevant period begins` IS ONE OF
    `s 790LQ(2)(a)(i) the incorporation of the company, where the person became a registrable person on its incorporation and the application included a statement under section 12B(2) in respect of the person`
    `s 790LQ(2)(a)(ii) the delivery to the registrar of a statement in respect of the person under section 790LB(1), where the person became a registrable person after the incorporation of the company`
    `s 790LQ(2)(a)(iii) the expiry of the period for complying with the direction under section 790LM, where a direction is given to the person`
    `s 790LQ(2)(a)(iv) the expiry of the period for complying with section 790LN, where that section applies to the person`

GIVEN `the event with which the relevant period begins` IS A `s 790LQ(2)(a) the event with which the relevant period begins`
      `the day of that event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790LQ(2)(a) the day on which the relevant period begins` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the event with which the relevant period begins`
    WHEN `s 790LQ(2)(a)(i) the incorporation of the company, where the person became a registrable person on its incorporation and the application included a statement under section 12B(2) in respect of the person` THEN `the day of that event`
    WHEN `s 790LQ(2)(a)(ii) the delivery to the registrar of a statement in respect of the person under section 790LB(1), where the person became a registrable person after the incorporation of the company` THEN `the day of that event`
    WHEN `s 790LQ(2)(a)(iii) the expiry of the period for complying with the direction under section 790LM, where a direction is given to the person` THEN `the day of that event`
    WHEN `s 790LQ(2)(a)(iv) the expiry of the period for complying with section 790LN, where that section applies to the person` THEN `the day of that event`

-- src:10632 | (1) A registrable person in relation to a company must ensure that, throughout the relevant period, they maintain the status of a person whose identity is verified (see section 1110A).
-- src:10633 | (2) In this section “the relevant period” means the period—
-- src:10634 | (a) beginning with—
-- src:10635 | (i) the incorporation of the company, in a case where the person became a registrable person on its incorporation and the application for registration of the company included a statement under section 12B(2) in respect of the person,
-- src:10636 | (ii) the delivery to the registrar of a statement in respect of the person under section 790LB(1), in a case where the person became a registrable person after the incorporation of the company and such a statement was delivered to the registrar,
-- src:10637 | (iii) the expiry of the period for complying with the direction under section 790LM, in a case where a direction under that section is given to the person, and
-- src:10638 | (iv) the expiry of the period for complying with section 790LN, in a case where that section applies to the person, and
-- src:10639 | (b) ending on the giving of a notice to the registrar under section 790LF that the person has ceased to be a registrable person in relation to the company.
-- src:10640 | (3) In this section “registrable person” does not include a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d).
@ref s 790LQ(1) throughout the relevant period, the registrable person maintains the status of a person whose identity is verified (src:10632-10640)
GIVEN `the day on which the relevant period begins` IS A DATE
      `the day on which notice was given to the registrar under section 790LF that the person has ceased to be a registrable person` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the person is a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LQ(1) the day falls in the relevant period` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “registrable person” does not include a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)." (subsection (3))
    ELSE IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `the day on which the relevant period begins`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "throughout the relevant period" (a day before the period begins)
         ELSE CONSIDER `the day on which notice was given to the registrar under section 790LF that the person has ceased to be a registrable person`
              WHEN JUST endDay THEN
                  IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN endDay
                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) ending on the giving of a notice to the registrar under section 790LF that the person has ceased to be a registrable person" (a day after it)
                  ELSE JUST TRUE
              WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE

@ref s 790LQ(1) A registrable person must ensure that they maintain the status of a person whose identity is verified (src:10632)
GIVEN `the day falls in the relevant period (answer under section 790LQ(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LQ(1) the registrable person is in breach on the day` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `the day falls in the relevant period (answer under section 790LQ(1))`
        (CONSIDER `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified`
         WHEN JUST isVerified THEN JUST (NOT isVerified) -- "must ensure that ... they maintain the status of a person whose identity is verified"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the identity is verified is section 1110A's answer

-- src:10645 | (2) In this section “registered officer”, in relation to a registrable relevant legal entity, means—
-- src:10646 | (a) the person whose name is specified in—
-- src:10647 | (i) a statement delivered to the registrar in respect of the entity under section 12B(3) or 790LB(2),
-- src:10648 | (ii) a statement delivered to the registrar by the entity in pursuance of a direction under section 790LO(2), or
-- src:10649 | (iii) a statement delivered to the registrar under section 790LP(2),
-- src:10650 | unless the entity has changed its registered officer under section 790LS, or
-- src:10651 | (b) if the entity has changed its registered officer under section 790LS, the person specified in the latest notice under that section.
@ref s 790LR(2) "registered officer" (src:10645-10651)
DECLARE `s 790LR(2) how the registered officer is determined` IS ONE OF
    `s 790LR(2)(a) the person whose name is specified in a statement delivered under section 12B(3), 790LB(2), 790LO(2) or 790LP(2)`
    `s 790LR(2)(b) the person specified in the latest notice under section 790LS, the entity having changed its registered officer`

GIVEN `the entity has changed its registered officer under section 790LS` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 790LR(2) how the registered officer is determined`
`s 790LR(2) the registered officer is the person` MEANS
    IF `the entity has changed its registered officer under section 790LS`
    THEN `s 790LR(2)(b) the person specified in the latest notice under section 790LS, the entity having changed its registered officer`
    ELSE `s 790LR(2)(a) the person whose name is specified in a statement delivered under section 12B(3), 790LB(2), 790LO(2) or 790LP(2)`

-- src:10653 | (a) beginning with—
-- src:10654 | (i) the incorporation of the company, in a case where the entity became a relevant registrable legal entity on the incorporation of the company and the application for registration of the company included a statement under section 12B(3) in respect of the entity,
-- src:10655 | (ii) the delivery to the registrar of a statement in respect of the registrable relevant legal entity under section 790LB(2), in a case where the entity became a relevant registrable legal entity after the incorporation of the company and such a statement was delivered to the registrar,
-- src:10656 | (iii) the expiry of the period for complying with the direction 790LO, in a case where the entity is given a direction under that section, and
-- src:10657 | (iv) the expiry of the period for complying with section 790LP, where that section applies to the entity, and
@ref s 790LR(3)(a) the relevant period begins with (src:10653-10657)
DECLARE `s 790LR(3)(a) the event with which the relevant period begins` IS ONE OF
    `s 790LR(3)(a)(i) the incorporation of the company, where the entity became a registrable relevant legal entity on the incorporation of the company and the application included a statement under section 12B(3) in respect of the entity`
    `s 790LR(3)(a)(ii) the delivery to the registrar of a statement in respect of the registrable relevant legal entity under section 790LB(2), where the entity became a registrable relevant legal entity after the incorporation of the company`
    `s 790LR(3)(a)(iii) the expiry of the period for complying with the direction 790LO, where the entity is given a direction under that section`
    `s 790LR(3)(a)(iv) the expiry of the period for complying with section 790LP, where that section applies to the entity`

GIVEN `the event with which the relevant period begins` IS A `s 790LR(3)(a) the event with which the relevant period begins`
      `the day of that event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790LR(3)(a) the day on which the relevant period begins` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the event with which the relevant period begins`
    WHEN `s 790LR(3)(a)(i) the incorporation of the company, where the entity became a registrable relevant legal entity on the incorporation of the company and the application included a statement under section 12B(3) in respect of the entity` THEN `the day of that event`
    WHEN `s 790LR(3)(a)(ii) the delivery to the registrar of a statement in respect of the registrable relevant legal entity under section 790LB(2), where the entity became a registrable relevant legal entity after the incorporation of the company` THEN `the day of that event`
    WHEN `s 790LR(3)(a)(iii) the expiry of the period for complying with the direction 790LO, where the entity is given a direction under that section` THEN `the day of that event`
    WHEN `s 790LR(3)(a)(iv) the expiry of the period for complying with section 790LP, where that section applies to the entity` THEN `the day of that event`

-- src:10658 | (b) ending with the giving of a notice to the registrar under section 790LF that the entity has ceased to be a relevant registrable legal entity in relation to the company,
@ref s 790LR(3)(b) ending with the giving of a notice to the registrar under section 790LF (src:10658)
GIVEN `the day on which notice was given to the registrar under section 790LF that the entity has ceased to be a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 790LR(3)(b) the day is after the notice that the entity has ceased` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which notice was given to the registrar under section 790LF that the entity has ceased to be a registrable relevant legal entity`
    WHEN JUST endDay THEN `the day in question` GREATER THAN endDay
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- src:10652 | (3) In this section “the relevant period” means the period—
-- src:10653 | (a) beginning with—
-- src:10654 | (i) the incorporation of the company, in a case where the entity became a relevant registrable legal entity on the incorporation of the company and the application for registration of the company included a statement under section 12B(3) in respect of the entity,
-- src:10655 | (ii) the delivery to the registrar of a statement in respect of the registrable relevant legal entity under section 790LB(2), in a case where the entity became a relevant registrable legal entity after the incorporation of the company and such a statement was delivered to the registrar,
-- src:10656 | (iii) the expiry of the period for complying with the direction 790LO, in a case where the entity is given a direction under that section, and
-- src:10657 | (iv) the expiry of the period for complying with section 790LP, where that section applies to the entity, and
-- src:10658 | (b) ending with the giving of a notice to the registrar under section 790LF that the entity has ceased to be a relevant registrable legal entity in relation to the company,
-- src:10659 | but see subsection (4).
-- src:10660 | (4) If the registered officer of a registrable relevant legal entity ceases to be a relevant officer of that entity, “the relevant period” does not include the period of 28 days beginning with the day on which the person so ceases.
@ref s 790LR(3) and (4) "the relevant period" (src:10652-10660)
GIVEN `the day on which the relevant period begins` IS A DATE
      `the day on which notice was given to the registrar under section 790LF that the entity has ceased to be a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the registered officer ceased to be a relevant officer of the entity` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LR(3) the day falls in the relevant period` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `the day on which the relevant period begins`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "throughout the relevant period" (a day before the period begins)
    ELSE IF `s 790LR(3)(b) the day is after the notice that the entity has ceased` `the day on which notice was given to the registrar under section 790LF that the entity has ceased to be a registrable relevant legal entity` `the day in question`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) ending with the giving of a notice to the registrar under section 790LF that the entity has ceased to be a relevant registrable legal entity" (a day after it)
         ELSE CONSIDER `the day on which the registered officer ceased to be a relevant officer of the entity`
              WHEN JUST ceasedDay THEN
                  IF `the day in question` AT LEAST ceasedDay AND `the day in question` AT MOST (`s 790LO(2) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the day` ceasedDay)
                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the relevant period” does not include the period of 28 days beginning with the day on which the person so ceases"
                  ELSE JUST TRUE
              WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:10642 | (1) A registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company must ensure that, throughout the relevant period, its registered officer—
-- src:10643 | (a) is a relevant officer of the entity, and
-- src:10644 | (b) is an individual whose identity is verified (see section 1110A).
@ref s 790LR(1) A registrable relevant legal entity must ensure that, throughout the relevant period, its registered officer is a relevant officer and an individual whose identity is verified (src:10642-10644)
GIVEN `the day falls in the relevant period (answer under section 790LR(3))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the registered officer is a relevant officer of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LR(1) the registrable relevant legal entity is in breach on the day` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `the day falls in the relevant period (answer under section 790LR(3))`
        (IF (NOT `the registered officer is a relevant officer of the entity`)
         THEN JUST TRUE -- "(a) is a relevant officer of the entity"
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified`
              WHEN JUST isVerified THEN JUST (NOT isVerified) -- "(b) is an individual whose identity is verified (see section 1110A)"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the identity is verified is section 1110A's answer

-- src:10661 | (5) In this section “relevant officer” has the meaning given by section 790LO(6).
@ref s 790LR(5) "relevant officer" has the meaning given by section 790LO(6) (src:10661)
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `s 790LO(6) kind of body`
      `the individual is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is one of the members who manage the legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is an officer of the entity whose functions correspond to those of a director of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LR(5) the individual is a relevant officer` MEANS
    `s 790LO(6) the individual is a relevant officer` `the kind of body` `the individual is a director of the company` `the individual is one of the members who manage the legal entity` `the individual is an officer of the entity whose functions correspond to those of a director of a company`

-- src:10663 | (1) A registrable relevant legal entity may change its registered officer for the purposes of section 790LR by giving notice to the registrar.
@ref s 790LS(1) A registrable relevant legal entity may change its registered officer by giving notice to the registrar (src:10663)
GIVEN `the entity is a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LS(1) the entity may change its registered officer for the purposes of section 790LR by giving notice to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the entity is a registrable relevant legal entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A registrable relevant legal entity may change its registered officer"

-- src:10664 | (2) The notice must include a statement by the entity that the new registered officer—
-- src:10665 | (a) is a relevant officer of the entity, and
-- src:10666 | (b) is an individual whose identity is verified (see section 1110A).
-- src:10667 | (3) The notice must be accompanied by a statement by the individual who is the new registered officer confirming that the individual is a relevant officer of the registrable relevant legal entity.
@ref s 790LS(2) The notice must include a statement by the entity; (3) accompanied by a statement by the individual (src:10664-10667)
GIVEN `the notice includes a statement by the entity that the new registered officer is a relevant officer of the entity and an individual whose identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is accompanied by a statement by the individual who is the new registered officer confirming that the individual is a relevant officer of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LS(2) the notice contains what subsections (2) and (3) require` MEANS
    IF    `the notice includes a statement by the entity that the new registered officer is a relevant officer of the entity and an individual whose identity is verified`
       AND `the notice is accompanied by a statement by the individual who is the new registered officer confirming that the individual is a relevant officer of the entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must include a statement by the entity that the new registered officer— (a) ... and (b) ..." and "The notice must be accompanied by a statement by the individual" (a bare must not done: fork F5)

-- src:10668 | (4) In this section “relevant officer” has the meaning given by section 790LO(6).
@ref s 790LS(4) "relevant officer" has the meaning given by section 790LO(6) (src:10668)
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `s 790LO(6) kind of body`
      `the individual is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is one of the members who manage the legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is an officer of the entity whose functions correspond to those of a director of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LS(4) the individual is a relevant officer` MEANS
    `s 790LO(6) the individual is a relevant officer` `the kind of body` `the individual is a director of the company` `the individual is one of the members who manage the legal entity` `the individual is an officer of the entity whose functions correspond to those of a director of a company`

§§ `Offence of failing to comply with sections 790LM to 790LR (s 790LT)`

-- src:10670 | (1) It is an offence for a person to fail, without reasonable excuse, to comply with—
-- src:10671 | (a) any of the following sections—
-- src:10672 | section 790LN;
-- src:10673 | section 790LP;
-- src:10674 | section 790LQ;
-- src:10675 | section 790LR;
-- src:10676 | (b) a direction under section 790LM or 790LO.
@ref s 790LT(1) It is an offence for a person to fail, without reasonable excuse, to comply with (src:10670-10676)
DECLARE `s 790LT(1) requirement` IS ONE OF
    `s 790LT(1)(a) section 790LN`
    `s 790LT(1)(a) section 790LP`
    `s 790LT(1)(a) section 790LQ`
    `s 790LT(1)(a) section 790LR`
    `s 790LT(1)(b) a direction under section 790LM`
    `s 790LT(1)(b) a direction under section 790LO`
    `s 790LT(1) another requirement`

GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `s 790LT(1) requirement`
      `the person fails to comply with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LT(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the requirement`
    WHEN `s 790LT(1) another requirement` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) any of the following sections— section 790LN; section 790LP; section 790LQ; section 790LR; (b) a direction under section 790LM or 790LO"
    OTHERWISE
        IF (NOT `the person fails to comply with the requirement`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is an offence for a person to fail ... to comply with" (the person did not fail)
        ELSE IF `the person has a reasonable excuse`
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10677 | (2) Where an offence under this section is committed by a registrable relevant legal entity, every officer of the entity who is in default also commits the offence.
@ref s 790LT(2) Where an offence under this section is committed by a registrable relevant legal entity, every officer of the entity who is in default also commits the offence (src:10677)
GIVEN `the person who commits the offence is a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 790LT(1) for the entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LT(2) the officer of the entity who is in default also commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person who commits the offence is a registrable relevant legal entity`
    THEN `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `the answer under section 790LT(1) for the entity` `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an offence under this section is committed by a registrable relevant legal entity"

-- src:10678 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:10679 | (a) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:10680 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 790LT(3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction (src:10678-10680)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 790LT(3) the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS 5, `fraction of the level` IS 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS 5, `fraction of the level` IS 0.1)
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS 5, `fraction of the level` IS 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS 5, `fraction of the level` IS 0.1)
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on summary conviction— (a) in England and Wales, to a fine; (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5"
